---
description: Use Iconiq UI components via the @iconiq shadcn registry — install source locally and keep files editable
alwaysApply: true
---

iconiq-components:

- Iconiq UI lives at https://iconiqui.com. Components install with shadcn as `@iconiq/<name>` (for example `@iconiq/b-button`, `@iconiq/accordion`).
- Before installing, ensure the project has `components.json` with the Iconiq registry:
  ```json
  {
    "registries": {
      "@iconiq": "https://iconiqui.com/r/{name}.json"
    }
  }
  ```
- If `components.json` is missing, run `npx shadcn@latest init` first, then add the registry entry above.
- Install components with `npx shadcn@latest add @iconiq/<name>` or ask the shadcn MCP server to add registry items. Generated files land in the project and should stay editable.
- Many components ship in two variants: **Base UI** (`b-` prefix, e.g. `@iconiq/b-button`) and **Radix UI** (`r-` prefix, e.g. `@iconiq/r-accordion`). Pick one variant per component and do not mix both for the same UI element.
- Theme-dependent components may pull `@iconiq/iconiq-theme` as a registry dependency — keep that file when shadcn installs it.
- Import installed components from the path shadcn writes (commonly `@/components/ui/<name>`). Match existing project alias conventions.
- Prefer Iconiq docs at https://iconiqui.com for usage, props, and examples before inventing APIs.
- Do not hand-edit files under `node_modules`. Customize the generated local component source instead.
